ic growth with 60% of India's  population involved in agriculture the  farming crisis does not bode well for  the prime minister but his decisive  action against terrorism and archrival  Pakistan earlier this year has given him  a boost as a strong leader national  security became the main focus and  further propelled Modi's popularity his  fate and that of 1.3 billion Indians  will be known next Thursday when results  are due whatever the outcome the  democratic process of getting hundreds  of millions to cast their vote for their  future is a clear winner never Lazarus  Sky News Delhi
 

